# denoiseai

- Label: Denoise AI
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 5
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/denoiseai.html
- Summary (EN): Applies a denoising library to an input layer. Supports Intel Open Image Denoise, shipped with Houdini, and NVIDIA OptiX, installed separately. Distinct from the Denoise TVD node.
- Résumé (FR) : Débruite une couche avec les bibliothèques Intel ou OptiX, guidées par les AOV de normales et d'albédo.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: image to denoise", "normal: normal AOV guiding noise reduction", "albedo: albedo AOV guiding noise reduction", "motionvec: motion vectors, required by OptiX for temporal noise removal", "prevframe: previous denoised frame, required by OptiX for temporal noise removal"]

- Key parameters: ["Denoiser: Intel or OptiX", "Auxiliary Planes Are Clean: sets the cleanAux filter when normal and albedo are already noise-free", "Prefilter Auxiliary Planes: cleans normal and albedo before denoising; better for final frames, slower", "Use CPU Only: forces the CPU device and reduces GPU memory use"]

- Caveats: ["Requires a supported platform and the chosen library installed.", "OptiX works only on NVIDIA cards and needs driver 435 or later.", "Prefiltering the auxiliary planes reduces performance; turn it off for previews."]

